{%- comment -%}
  On the product page below 900px this bar stands down by default, because the
  sticky buy bar carries the same promises one line above the Add to Cart —
  where a shopper is actually deciding — and two copies of "free shipping" on
  one screen is one copy too many. It is worth 32px of permanent viewport on
  the longest, most fold-constrained page in the theme, on the template where
  the photograph already takes a full screen width of height.

  A setting rather than a hard rule: a merchant who puts something here that
  is not a trust fact — a sale, a shipping cut-off, a festival message — needs
  it read on every template, and can switch it back on.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="announce{% unless settings.pdp_announce_mobile %} announce--stand-down{% endunless %}" role="region" aria-label="Store information">
  <span class="inner narrow">{{ section.settings.item_1 }}<span class="sep">&middot;</span>{{ section.settings.item_2 }}</span>
  <span class="inner wide">{{ section.settings.item_1 }}<span class="sep">&middot;</span>{{ section.settings.item_2 }}<span class="sep">&middot;</span>{{ section.settings.item_3 }}</span>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Announcement bar",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "item_1", "label": "Item 1 (always shown)", "default": "Free Shipping Across India" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "item_2", "label": "Item 2 (always shown)", "default": "Cash on Delivery" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "item_3", "label": "Item 3 (wide screens only)", "default": "Safe & Soft XPE Foam" }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}